  1307      Note that in contrast with BCFv2.1 specification, HTSlib implementation
  1308      allows missing values in vectors. For integer types, the values 0x80,
  1309      0x8000, 0x80000000 are interpreted as missing values and 0x81, 0x8001,
  1310      0x80000001 as end-of-vector indicators.  Similarly for floats, the value of
  1311      0x7F800001 is interpreted as a missing value and 0x7F800002 as an
  1312      end-of-vector indicator.
  1313      Note that the end-of-vector byte is not part of the vector.
  1314
  1315      This trial BCF version (v2.2) is compatible with the VCF specification and
  1316      enables to handle correctly vectors with different ploidy in presence of
  1317      missing values.
  1318   */
